Implement reusable bounded free associative algebra over existing BigPoly commuting coefficients.
Public OrderedPolynomial has private BTreeMap<Vec<String>,BigPoly>, canonical zero omission.
API: scalar(BigPoly,&mut Budget), generator(&str,&mut Budget), terms() borrowed map;
try_add/sub/mul(&self,&Self,&mut Budget), try_scale(&self,&BigPoly,&mut Budget),
try_neg(&self,&mut Budget), commutator(&self,&Self,&mut Budget),
truncate(&self,parameters:&[&str],max_degree:usize,&mut Budget),
coefficient(&self,parameter:&str,power:usize,&mut Budget),
substitute(&self,&BTreeMap<String,Self>,&mut Budget). All constructors and transformations
return computation::Result<Self>. Derive Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq.
Words concatenate without sorting; scalars commute; commutator is XY-YX.
Truncation selects total degree only in named commuting parameters; coefficient removes
exact requested power of one commuting parameter. Substitution is simultaneous,
nonrecursive, operator-only; missing replacements remain generators.
Validate every raw name and replacement even for zero input. Names must be nonempty
and contain no whitespace/control characters. Use only checked BigPoly arithmetic.
Before allocating growing keys/maps, check aggregate word occurrences, coefficient
monomials, symbol UTF8 bytes, coefficient bits, terms, degrees, and charged work.
Bound words and coefficient degree with hard caps independent of caller limits to
bound BTreeMap recursive key destruction stack. Operations are iterative. Reject
conservatively before temporary growth; cancellation need not rescue an over-budget
candidate. No implicit Lorentz relations or special problem letters. Test full word
Jacobi expansion, noncommutativity, first-order inverse conjugation and signs,
simultaneous substitution, invalid names/zero inputs, resource boundaries, >i128.
Manual prompt-first implementation authorized after prior provider rejection;
no model generation or successful automatic PDD synchronization claimed.
Resource semantics: Terms counts aggregate coefficient monomials, InputBytes counts
all stored operator and commuting symbol occurrences, CoefficientBits sums maximum
component bits across Gaussian coefficients. WordLength is per word; aggregate word
storage is bounded by max_terms*max_word_length as well as aggregate bytes/work.
Hard word/commuting-degree cap is 256. Charge name byte scanning and parameter
membership scans. Replacement map key bytes plus all replacement symbol bytes
must fit one combined input-byte cap, even if the source expression is zero.
Product admission may use a conservative four-times sum-of-component-bits estimate;
reject temporary Cartesian expansion before growth even if cancellation would fit.
